---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const lastUpdated = "August 22, 2026";
---

<Layout 
  title="Privacy Policy | Dino Run: Epochs" 
  description="Learn how Dino Run: Epochs collects, protects, and manages data. Read our Google AdSense, cookie, GDPR, CCPA, and COPPA compliance policy."
>
  <Header activePage="privacy" />

  <main class="content-page">
    <div class="section-container">
      <div class="content-hero">
        <span class="badge">Legal & Compliance</span>
        <h1>Privacy <span class="gradient-text">Policy</span></h1>
        <p>Your privacy is paramount to us. This policy details our data practices, cookie policies, and regulatory compliance standards.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-dim); margin-top: 10px;">Last Updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="content-body">
        <div class="info-callout">
          <p><strong>Summary for Gamers:</strong> Dino Run: Epochs does not require an account or collect personal identifying information (PII) like names or passwords to play. Your high scores and coins are stored privately in your own browser via LocalStorage. Third-party advertising partners like Google AdSense may use cookies to serve relevant advertisements.</p>
        </div>

        <h2>1. Overview and Scope</h2>
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy describes the policies and procedures of <strong>Dino Run: Epochs</strong> ("we", "us", or "our") regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of information when you access or play our web game at <a href="https://dino-run-epochs.vercel.app" style="color: var(--accent-cyan);">dino-run-epochs.vercel.app</a> (the "Website" or "Service").
        </p>
        <p>
          By using our Website, you consent to the data collection and usage practices described in this policy. If you do not agree with any terms, please discontinue using the Service.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Information We Collect and Store</h2>
        <p>We believe in minimal data collection. We categorize the data associated with your gameplay as follows:</p>

        <h3>A. Browser LocalStorage (Game State)</h3>
        <p>
          To provide a persistent gaming experience, Dino Run: Epochs stores non-personal game progress data directly inside your browser's <code>localStorage</code>. This data includes:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>High Scores:</strong> Your local best survival score and epoch distance records.</li>
          <li><strong>Coin Count:</strong> Collected gold coins used for unlocking dinosaur skins in the in-game shop.</li>
          <li><strong>Audio & Settings Preferences:</strong> Music volume, sound effects toggle, and graphical settings.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><em>Note: This data is stored locally on your device and is never transmitted to or stored on our external servers. You can clear this data at any time by clearing your browser's cache and site data.</em></p>

        <h3>B. Automated Log Data & Analytics</h3>
        <p>
          When you visit our site, our hosting and analytics providers (such as Vercel Analytics and Vercel Speed Insights) may automatically collect standard web log metrics, including:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Browser type, engine, and version (e.g., Chrome, Safari, Firefox).</li>
          <li>Device category and operating system (Windows, macOS, Android, iOS).</li>
          <li>Referrer URL and navigation timestamps.</li>
          <li>Core Web Vitals performance metrics (Largest Contentful Paint, First Input Delay, Cumulative Layout Shift).</li>
        </ul>
        <p>This information is processed in aggregate and anonymized form solely to monitor server stability, optimize frame rates, and improve website performance.</p>

        <h2>3. Third-Party Advertising & Google AdSense</h2>
        <p>
          We use <strong>Google AdSense</strong> to display advertisements when you visit our website. Google, as a third-party vendor, uses cookies and web beacons to serve ads based on your prior visits to our website or other websites on the Internet.
        </p>

        <div class="content-card">
          <h3>DoubleClick DART Cookies & Google Ad Policies</h3>
          <p>
            Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to our users based on their visit to our site and/or other sites on the Internet.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to this website or other websites.</li>
            <li>Users may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-cyan); font-weight: 600;">Google Ads Settings</a>.</li>
            <li>Alternatively, you can opt out of third-party vendor cookies for personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-cyan); font-weight: 600;">www.aboutads.info</a>.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h2>4. Cookie Management and Opt-Outs</h2>
        <p>
          Cookies are small text files placed on your device by web browsers. You have full control over cookie permissions:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>You can configure your browser settings to reject all cookies, notify you when a cookie is issued, or delete cookies at any time.</li>
          <li>If you choose to disable cookies, some interactive website features may not operate as intended, but core offline gameplay will remain playable.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. GDPR Compliance (General Data Protection Regulation)</h2>
        <p>
          If you are a resident of the European Economic Area (EEA), you possess statutory rights regarding your personal information under the GDPR:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>The Right to Access:</strong> You have the right to request copies of your personal data held by us.</li>
          <li><strong>The Right to Rectification:</strong> You have the right to request correction of inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
          <li><strong>The Right to Erasure (Right to be Forgotten):</strong> You have the right to request that we erase your data under certain conditions.</li>
          <li><strong>The Right to Restrict or Object to Processing:</strong> You have the right to object to or restrict processing of your personal data.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Since we do not store server-side personal accounts or identifying databases, clearing your browser's local storage and cookies immediately removes all records linked to your browser session.</p>

        <h2>6. CCPA / CPRA Disclosures (California Consumer Privacy Act)</h2>
        <p>
          Under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) and California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA), California consumers have specific privacy rights:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Right to Know:</strong> You may request disclosure of the categories and specific pieces of personal information collected over the preceding 12 months.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Delete:</strong> You may request deletion of personal information collected from you.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Opt-Out of the Sale/Sharing of Personal Information:</strong> We do not sell personal data for monetary consideration. For ad personalization opt-outs, please refer to Google Ads Settings.</li>
          <li><strong>Non-Discrimination:</strong> We will not discriminate against you for exercising your CCPA privacy rights.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>7. Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA)</h2>
        <p>
          Protecting the privacy of young children is especially important. Dino Run: Epochs is designed as a family-friendly, general audience entertainment game.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>We do not knowingly collect, request, or solicit any personally identifiable information from children under the age of 13.</li>
          <li>If we learn that we have inadvertently collected personal information from a child under 13 without verifiable parental consent, we will promptly delete such information from our records.</li>
          <li>If you are a parent or guardian and believe your child has provided us with personal data, please contact us immediately.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>8. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update our Privacy Policy periodically to reflect changes in regulatory standards, legal requirements, or game features. Any changes will be posted directly on this page with an updated "Last Updated" revision date. We encourage you to review this Privacy Policy periodically.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Contact Us</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions, feedback, or concerns regarding this Privacy Policy or our privacy practices, please contact us:
        </p>
        <div class="content-card">
          <p><strong>Dino Run: Epochs Privacy Team</strong></p>
          <p>Email: <a href="mailto:privacy@dinorunepochs.com" style="color: var(--accent-cyan);">privacy@dinorunepochs.com</a></p>
          <p>Online Form: <a href="/contact" style="color: var(--accent-cyan);">Contact & Support Page</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
